            "result_text": "Done! The regex pattern has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\n**Pattern breakdown:**\n\n- **IPv4 validation**: `(?:(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4][0-9]|1[0-9]{2}|[1-9][0-9]|[0-9])\\.){3}...` matches 0-255 per octet without leading zeros\n  \n- **Date validation with correct day ranges**:\n  - 31-day months (Jan, Mar, May, Jul, Aug, Oct, Dec): day 01-31\n  - 30-day months (Apr, Jun, Sep, Nov): day 01-30  \n  - February: day 01-29\n  \n- **Last date only**: The negative lookahead `(?!.*\\b...\\b)` ensures the captured date is the last one in the line\n\n- **Word boundaries**: `\\b` before and after IPv4 and dates prevents false matches like \"user1134-12-1234\"\n\nThe regex works with `re.findall(pattern, text, re.MULTILINE)` to extract the last date from each line containing a valid IPv4 address."
